#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:218
msgid "Show rulers"
msgstr "Vertoon lineale"

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:219
msgid ""
"This is checked by default and both a vertical and horizontal ruler are shown "
"on KPresenter slide. When unchecked, the rulers are not shown anymore on any "
"slide."
msgstr ""

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:223
msgid "Show status bar"
msgstr "Vertoon status kolom"

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:224
msgid "Toggle the statusbar which is shown by default."
msgstr ""

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:231
msgid "Number of recent files:"
msgstr "Nommer van onlangse lêers:"

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:232
msgid ""
"Set the number of recent files which will be opened using the File->"
"Open Recent menu. Default is to remember 10 filenames. The maximum you can set "
"is 20 and the minimum is 1."
msgstr ""

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:243
msgid "Text indentation depth:"
msgstr ""

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:244
msgid ""
"This setting is used in the Text menu by Increase Depth and Decrease Depth menu "
"items to change the indentation depth. Default is 1 centimeter."
msgstr ""

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:314
#, fuzzy
msgid "Background object color:"
msgstr "Agtergrond kleur:"

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:315
msgid ""
"Change the background color of the text box. The Text boxes background is white "
"by default. If you had a dark background color and you wanted to put some white "
"text over it, you could color the text box so that you could see what you were "
"typing. When you have finished, the area around the text would revert to "
"whatever the background color was. The Defaults button restores the original "
"settings."
msgstr ""

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:326
msgid "Grid color:"
msgstr "Rooster kleur:"

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:327
msgid "You can change here the grid color which is black as default."
msgstr ""

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:424
msgid "Undo/redo limit:"
msgstr "Herstel/herstel herroep beperk:"

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:426
msgid ""
"Set the number of actions you can undo and redo (how many actions KPresenter "
"keeps in its Undo buffer). Default is 30. Maximum is 60 and minimum is 0. Any "
"action that exceeds the number set will be forgotten."
msgstr ""

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:431
msgid "Display links"
msgstr "Vertoon skakel"

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:432
msgid ""
"When you want to include a link in your slide, you will use the Insert->"
"Link... menu which allows you to insert URL, mail or file links. If the option "
"Display links is checked, all links will be displayed in a different color. "
"This makes document links visible. This is the default behavior. If the option "
"is unchecked, the link will be the same color as the text color. The links are "
"visible(or not) both in the edited slides and in the slide show."
msgstr ""

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:436
msgid "&Underline all links"
msgstr "Onderstreep alle skakel"

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:438
msgid ""
"If this is checked, all links will be underlined. The option is checked per "
"default. If it is not checked, the link will not be underlined."
msgstr ""

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:442
msgid "Display comments"
msgstr "Vertoon kommentaar"

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:444
msgid ""
"Comments are inserted in the text at the cursor using the Insert->"
"Comment... menu. Comments can only be viewed in editing mode and not in the "
"slide show. If this option is checked (default) then each comment will be shown "
"as a small yellow rectangle. You can then right click on it to edit it, remove "
"it or copy its text."
msgstr ""

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:447
msgid "Display field code"
msgstr "Vertoon veld kode"

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:449
msgid ""
"In editor mode (not in slide show) this option will display all the variable "
"codes as well as Link at links location. This is very useful to see what "
"variable is displayed. Variables are inserted using the Insert -> "
"Variable menu."
msgstr ""

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:452
msgid "Print slide notes"
msgstr ""

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:454
msgid ""
"If checked, all notes will be printed on paper. The notes will all be printed "
"on a separate last page, from slide one to the last slide and fifnishing with "
"the Master Page Note. You can see the notes for each slide using the View->"
"Show notebar menu."
msgstr ""

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:459
msgid "Grid"
msgstr "Rooster"

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:465
#, fuzzy
msgid "Horizontal grid size:"
msgstr "Horisontaal Gradiënt"

#: kpresenter_dlg_config.cc:466
msgid ""
"Set the space in millimeters between two horizontal points on the grid. Default "
"is 5 millimeters."
msgstr ""

